      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Two-character workflow (regional prompting)\n\nEach character gets its own prompt that only applies to part of the image, so features stop bleeding between them (for example horns appearing on both people).\n\n- Shared prompt: scene, style, composition, and the count tags (1girl, 1boy).\n- Left character: applies to the left 65% of the image.\n- Right character: applies to the right 65%. The 30% overlap in the middle lets them touch or hug.\n- The character prompts switch on at 20% of sampling (Timestep Range nodes), after the shared prompt has laid out the composition. Raise start to 0.3 if the characters drift apart; lower it to 0.1 if features still bleed.\n- Area strength 0.8: higher makes each character follow its prompt more strictly.\n\nTo swap sides, swap the two prompts. To change the split, edit width and x in the area nodes (for example 0.6 / 0.0 and 0.6 / 0.4).\n\nUse landscape sizes (1216x832 or 1344x768) so both fit side by side. If a face needs fixing, run the result through fix_faces with that character's prompt.\n\nLimits: regions are rectangles, so characters that heavily overlap (one directly in front of the other) can still mix. Keep each character's distinctive tags (hair colour, horns, outfit) only in their own prompt."
      ]
    },
